WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.120
Whoa.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.280
You've just come out of Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:04.310
You've cheered at all the fights.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:05.470
Laughed at all the jokes.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.550
You've been shaken, speechless and sobbing.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:09.860
You've made an appointment for therapy for
tomorrow.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.780
Don't worry...we're all right there with you.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.590
There's only one cure for the post-Infinity
War blues, and that's diving straight into

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.380
the ending and trying to figure out what the
hell just happened, and what the hell is going

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:19.960
to happen next.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.280
Strap in, put your helmet on, and prepare
your haunches, people.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.880
Here's the ending of Avengers: Infinity War
explained.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.540
And of course, gigantic, earth-shattering
spoilers ahead.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.200
Last chance to turn back...

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.360
So...what just happened?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.860
Thanos won!

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:35.440
Can you believe it?

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.400
The bad guy beat the good guys and it's totally
mind-blowing because that kinda never happens!

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.100
But it did this time, and it was just about
perfect.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.420
Thanos managed to assemble all six of the
Infinity Stones, sacrificing his own adopted

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.320
daughter in the process, snapped his fingers,
and poof.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.360
Game over, man.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.000
Of course, fans of the comics and MCU-followers
probably knew going into the movie that there

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.500
was a good chance Thanos would be victorious
before the final credits rolled.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.540
Longtime comic book readers have the image
of Thanos snapping his fingers with a fully

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.960
powered Infinity Gauntlet on his hand burned
into their brains, so it only makes sense

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.780
that one of the most iconic moments in all
of Marvel Comics history would show up in

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.360
this film.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:16.660
On top of that, we all knew that Marvel would
be splitting the story into two movies, even

00:01:16.670 --> 00:01:19.869
if they later publicly reversed course on
that particular point.

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:23.929
In the end, if you didn't know that Thanos
might pull out the W by the end of this movie,

00:01:23.929 --> 00:01:25.600
you haven't been paying close attention.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.120
Body count

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:31.439
When it comes to writing about comic book
movies, it's pretty fun to try and predict

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:34.490
who will live and who will die when the next
big flick hits the theaters.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:38.479
In fact, making these kinds of predictions
is basically how some YouTube channels go

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.060
about building their whole business.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:40.960
wink wink

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.620
But even still, no one could've quite predicted
just how many hugely important superheroic

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.850
characters would go off to that big comic
book store in the sky by the end of Infinity

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:50.340
War.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.440
For those keeping score at home, we lost Bucky,
Black Panther, Scarlet Witch, Falcon, Drax,

00:01:55.459 --> 00:02:01.709
Doctor Strange, Spider-Man, Star-Lord, Mantis,
Groot, Nick Fury, and Maria Hill, and those

00:02:01.709 --> 00:02:05.539
are just the characters we saw dissolve after
Thanos pulled his big trick.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.160
It was a lot.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.910
And that's not even a complete list of all
the dead people.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:13.490
Right off the bat, Heimdall and Loki died
at Thanos's hands, while Gamora and Vision

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.080
went down for the count as well.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.980
After ten years and 18 movies, the Marvel
Cinematic Universe built up a huge roster

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.920
of memorable and important characters.

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.880
While it goes without saying that the vast
majority of these dead people will not stay

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:30.110
dead by the time the fourth Avengers movie
debuts, it's hard not to feel the loss of

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:33.380
so many characters we've gotten to know over
the years.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.280
Where did Thanos talk to Gamora?

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:40.310
Towards the end of the film, Thanos appeared
in an orangey, reddish place, and began talking

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.570
with a version of Gamora who looked like a
child.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:45.740
We'd never seen that place before in the film...so
where was he?

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.700
There's a more than decent chance that he
was inside the orange Soul Stone itself.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.040
Thanos sacrificed Gamora to obtain the Soul
Stone, and so it makes sense that she and

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.280
the Stone would be connected somehow after
her death.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:00.500
And in the various comics concerning Thanos
and his quest for the Infinity Stones, the

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.580
Soul Gem wound up playing host to a few characters
who died fighting Thanos, including Gamora.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:09.640
And with that in mind, it's entirely possible
that all our dead heroes may have had their

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.200
souls transported to the Soul Stone as well.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.940
Doctor Strange's prescription for victory

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:20.080
Early on, Doctor Strange told Iron Man that
if it came down to possibly saving him or

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.820
protecting the Time Stone, he'd choose the
Stone.

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:27.640
Then, around the midpoint of the film, Doctor
Strange used the Eye of Agamotto to explore

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:32.650
over 14 million possible battles against Thanos,
looking for the path to victory.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:37.500
In all of those possible futures, he only
saw one where the good guys came out on top.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.680
It sure sounded dire.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.840
But when Thanos threatened to kill Iron Man
on Titan, Doctor Strange offered the Time

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.580
Stone to save Tony Stark's life.

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.960
When Iron Man called him out on it later,
he said it was "the only way."

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:48.860
Say what?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.060
Well, it all makes sense if you think about
it.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:55.140
Doctor Strange has some experience using his
time powers to cheat his way out of some bad

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:55.960
situations.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:57.280
"Dormmamu!'

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:00.900
"Dormmamu, I've come to bargain!"

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:01.900
"Dormmamu!'

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.980
"Dormmamu!'

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:03.540
"Dormmamu!'

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.880
This time around, he took a peek at the script
for the next Avengers movie and realized that

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:13.660
it was important that Iron Man live to the
end, important enough that he gave up the

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.340
Time Stone to make sure it happens.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.299
And considering that Iron Man is the one who
kicked off this whole crazy Marvel Cinematic

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:23.360
Universe in the first place, it only makes
sense that he'd be pretty necessary to finishing

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.560
things off over a decade later.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.700
Nebula's revenge

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:30.900
Among the movie's survivors was Thanos' least
favorite daughter, Nebula.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:35.160
She managed to make it to the end of the movie
despite being literally dissected earlier

00:04:35.169 --> 00:04:36.169
in the film.

00:04:36.169 --> 00:04:40.159
So why would a scrub like Nebula be alive
while so many fan-favorite characters got

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:41.020
turned to dust?

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.800
As with so many things, the answer lies in
the comics.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:48.600
In the Infinity Gauntlet comic book storyline,
Nebula spent a lot of time shambling around

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:52.099
as a creepy zombie lady, a victim of Thanos'
power.

00:04:52.099 --> 00:04:56.430
But at one point in the story, Thanos was
distracted by an encounter with Eternity,

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.189
a cosmic being that represented the universe
itself.

00:04:59.189 --> 00:05:03.800
That's when Nebula grabbed his fancy glove
for herself, and contributed to his eventual

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:04.300
undoing.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.940
Don't be surprised if the MCU version of Nebula
winds up fulfilling a similar role in the

00:05:08.949 --> 00:05:10.500
next Avengers movie, too.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.220
Paging Captain Marvel…

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.860
In the movie's one post-credits scene, we
saw the long-awaited return of Nick Fury and

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:19.520
Maria Hill trying to get in touch with somebody.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:23.900
Given that we'd spent a full movie not seeing
Hawkeye shooting arrows at anybody, it seemed

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:27.300
like a foregone conclusion that he was the
guy Fury was trying to reach.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:31.779
But as it turned out, he was actually trying
to get in touch with Captain Marvel.

00:05:31.779 --> 00:05:36.180
Fans of the Marvel Cinematic Universe know
that Brie Larson is all set to debut as the

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:41.629
MCU's first female-fronted superhero movie
in March, 2019, a couple months before the

00:05:41.629 --> 00:05:43.320
release of the next Avengers movie.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:48.380
Interestingly, Captain Marvel is supposedly
going to take place in the 1990s, meaning

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:52.020
that the superhero who shows up to save the
day in the fourth Avengers will have already

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.620
been established in some capacity for years.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.560
So where's she been for all the other super-shenanigans
over the last bunch of movies?

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.260
About Hawkeye...

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.520
We never did get a glimpse of Hawkeye after
all, meaning everyone's favorite archer is

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:07.120
surely going to show up in the next Avengers
movie, right?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.819
He's a necessary part of the team!

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:14.400
"The city is flying, we're fighting an army
of robots, and I have a bow and arrow.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.620
None of this makes sense."

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:21.180
Okay, maybe he's not that necessary, but still,
every hero helps, right?

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:24.160
Is his family okay in the aftermath of Thanos'
dirty deeds?

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:28.610
Could he possibly be looking to...avenge them,
and everyone else on Earth, perhaps?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:31.460
"If we can't protect the earth, you can be
damn sure we'll avenge it."

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:32.940
Thanks for watching!

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.720
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:35.729 --> 00:06:37.979
Plus, check out all this other cool stuff
we know you'll love too.

